---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How Brain Seal Ltd handles privacy across its video games, website and related services.">
  <PageHeader eyebrow="Legal" title="Privacy Policy">
    <p>Brain Seal Ltd · Last updated: 3 November 2026</p>
  </PageHeader>
  <article class="section">
    <div class="wrap legal">
      <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
      <p>Brain Seal Ltd ("Brain Seal", "we", "us" or "our") is an independent video game developer and publisher based in the United Kingdom.</p>
      <p>We respect your privacy and believe that enjoying a video game should not require you to surrender your personal information.</p>
      <p>This Privacy Policy explains how privacy is handled across our video games, website and related services.</p>
      <p>
        It applies to all games developed or published by Brain Seal, including the Dark Quest series, Story of a Gladiator, Geometry Survivor,
        Monarchy, Blow it up and Dominus Gladiatus, as well as our website at <a href="https://brainseal.com">https://brainseal.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Privacy in Our Games</h2>
      <p>Brain Seal does not collect personal information from players through its video games.</p>
      <p>Our games do not collect or transmit personal data to Brain Seal for analytics, advertising, user profiling or behavioural tracking.</p>
      <p>Specifically, Brain Seal does not:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Collect players' names, email addresses or contact details through gameplay.</li>
        <li>Track individual gameplay behaviour for analytics or marketing.</li>
        <li>Collect advertising identifiers.</li>
        <li>Sell or share player information with data brokers or advertisers.</li>
        <li>Operate personalised advertising or behavioural profiling systems within its games.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Game progress, settings and saved games may be stored locally on your device or through storage services provided by the platform on which you play.</p>
      <p>Information managed by third-party gaming platforms is subject to their respective privacy policies.</p>

      <h2>3. Gaming Platforms and Third-Party Services</h2>
      <p>Our games are available through third-party digital distribution services, including:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Steam, operated by Valve Corporation.</li>
        <li>PlayStation and PlayStation Network, operated by Sony Interactive Entertainment.</li>
        <li>Xbox and associated Microsoft services.</li>
        <li>Nintendo eShop and associated Nintendo services.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These companies may independently collect and process information relating to your account, purchases, achievements, cloud saves, device or use of their services.</p>
      <p>Brain Seal does not control the independent data-processing practices of these platform providers.</p>
      <p>We encourage players to consult the applicable platform privacy policy:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Steam: <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/privacy_agreement/" rel="noopener">https://store.steampowered.com/privacy_agreement/</a></li>
        <li>PlayStation: <a href="https://www.playstation.com/legal/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">https://www.playstation.com/legal/privacy-policy/</a></li>
        <li>Microsoft: <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" rel="noopener">https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement</a></li>
        <li>Nintendo: <a href="https://www.nintendo.com/privacy-policy/" rel="noopener">https://www.nintendo.com/privacy-policy/</a></li>
      </ul>
      <p>Platform features such as cloud saves and achievements may involve information being processed by the relevant platform, even though Brain Seal does not independently collect that information.</p>

      <h2>4. Our Website</h2>
      <p>Our official website provides information about Brain Seal and its games.</p>
      <p>We do not use the website to profile visitors or collect personal information for advertising or behavioural analytics.</p>
      <p>
        However, the infrastructure used to deliver a website may automatically process limited technical information, such as IP addresses, request
        timestamps and browser information, for operational and security purposes.
      </p>
      <p>Such processing may be performed by our website hosting or infrastructure providers.</p>
      <p>
        Where Brain Seal determines the purposes of any personal data processing, the lawful basis is our legitimate interest in maintaining a
        functional, reliable and secure website, subject to applicable data protection law.
      </p>
      <p>We do not use personal information obtained through our website for personalised advertising.</p>
      <p>Our website may link to or display content from third-party services, including game storefronts and video platforms. Those services may process information under their own privacy policies.</p>

      <h2>5. Cookies and Tracking Technologies</h2>
      <p>Brain Seal does not use cookies or similar technologies for personalised advertising or behavioural tracking.</p>
      <p>Technical cookies or comparable technologies may be used where necessary for website functionality or security.</p>
      <p>
        If we introduce optional analytics or other non-essential tracking technologies in the future, we will update this Policy and implement any
        notices, consent mechanisms or other controls required by applicable law.
      </p>
      <p>Third-party websites and embedded services may use their own cookies or similar technologies, subject to their respective policies.</p>

      <h2>6. Contacting Brain Seal</h2>
      <p>Although our games do not collect personal information, you may voluntarily provide information when contacting us by email.</p>
      <p>This may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Your email address.</li>
        <li>Your name, if provided.</li>
        <li>The contents of your message.</li>
        <li>Attachments or technical information you voluntarily submit.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We use this information solely to respond to enquiries, provide customer support, resolve reported problems, conduct legitimate business
        correspondence or meet applicable legal obligations.
      </p>
      <p>
        The lawful basis for this processing may be our legitimate interests in responding to communications, performance of a contract where
        applicable, or compliance with a legal obligation.
      </p>
      <p>We do not use support correspondence to create advertising profiles or send unsolicited marketing communications.</p>
      <p>
        Correspondence is retained only for as long as reasonably necessary for its purpose, taking account of follow-up enquiries, relevant legal
        requirements and potential disputes. We periodically review information held and delete it when no longer required.
      </p>
      <p>Our email service providers may process communications on our behalf under appropriate contractual and security arrangements.</p>

      <h2>7. Sharing of Personal Information</h2>
      <p>Brain Seal does not sell personal information.</p>
      <p>
        Personal information voluntarily provided through correspondence may be shared with service providers assisting with email, technical support
        or other necessary business operations, subject to appropriate safeguards.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may also disclose information where required by applicable law, valid legal process or a competent public authority, or where reasonably
        necessary to establish, exercise or defend legal rights.
      </p>
      <p>We do not disclose personal information to third parties for their independent advertising or behavioural profiling purposes.</p>

      <h2>8. International Processing</h2>
      <p>Brain Seal is established in the United Kingdom and provides its games internationally.</p>
      <p>Personal information contained in voluntary communications or processed through website infrastructure may be handled by service providers operating in other countries.</p>
      <p>
        Where international transfers are subject to the UK GDPR or EU GDPR, applicable legal transfer requirements must be satisfied. These may
        include adequacy decisions, approved contractual safeguards or another lawful transfer mechanism.
      </p>
      <p>Information processed independently by digital gaming platforms is governed by those platforms' respective arrangements and privacy notices.</p>

      <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
      <p>We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect any personal information received through correspondence or processed in connection with our website.</p>
      <p>Access is restricted to authorised individuals and service providers where necessary.</p>
      <p>
        No electronic communication or storage system can be guaranteed to be entirely secure, but we seek to apply measures appropriate to the nature
        of the information and the risks involved.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p>Our video games do not collect personal information from children through Brain Seal-operated gameplay tracking or analytics systems.</p>
      <p>We do not knowingly use children's personal information for behavioural advertising or profiling.</p>
      <p>Gaming platforms may independently process account information and operate parental controls, age restrictions and other child-safety features.</p>
      <p>
        Parents or guardians who believe that personal information has been provided to Brain Seal inappropriately may contact us to request its
        review or deletion, where applicable.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Your Data Protection Rights</h2>
      <p>
        Where Brain Seal processes your personal information, you may have rights under the UK General Data Protection Regulation, EU General Data
        Protection Regulation or other applicable privacy legislation.
      </p>
      <p>Depending on the circumstances, these include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>The right to request access to your personal information.</li>
        <li>The right to request correction of inaccurate information.</li>
        <li>The right to request deletion of information where legally applicable.</li>
        <li>The right to request restriction of certain processing.</li>
        <li>The right to object to processing based on legitimate interests.</li>
        <li>The right to data portability where applicable.</li>
        <li>The right to withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These rights are subject to applicable legal requirements and exceptions.</p>
      <p>Because Brain Seal does not collect personal information directly through its games, we may not hold player information associated with a particular game account.</p>
      <p>Requests relating to information independently held by Steam, PlayStation, Xbox or Nintendo should be directed to the relevant platform provider.</p>
      <p>To exercise rights concerning information held by Brain Seal, contact <a href="mailto:support@brainseal.com">support@brainseal.com</a>.</p>
      <p>We will respond in accordance with applicable legal time limits and may request information reasonably necessary to verify your identity.</p>

      <h2>12. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p>We may revise this Privacy Policy to reflect changes to our games, website, services or applicable laws.</p>
      <p>The current version will be published at:<br /><a href="https://brainseal.com/privacy-policy/">https://brainseal.com/privacy-policy/</a></p>
      <p>The date at the beginning of this document indicates when it was last updated.</p>
      <p>Where legally required, we will provide additional notice of material changes.</p>

      <h2>13. Complaints</h2>
      <p>If you have a concern regarding how Brain Seal handles personal information, please contact us so that we can investigate.</p>
      <p>You may also lodge a complaint with the relevant data protection supervisory authority.</p>
      <p>In the United Kingdom, this is the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO):<br /><a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">https://ico.org.uk</a></p>
      <p>Individuals in the European Economic Area may have the right to lodge complaints with an appropriate national data protection authority.</p>

      <h2>14. Company and Contact Information</h2>
      <address>
        Brain Seal Ltd<br />
        Company number: 06334639<br />
        Registered in England and Wales<br />
        207 Regent Street, 3rd Floor<br />
        London, W1B 3HH<br />
        United Kingdom<br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:support@brainseal.com">support@brainseal.com</a><br />
        Website: <a href="https://brainseal.com">https://brainseal.com</a>
      </address>
      <p>For privacy enquiries, please include "Privacy Request" in the subject line.</p>
      <p class="copyright">© 2026 Brain Seal Ltd. All rights reserved.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>

